{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9cbtrbiet","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"GOTCHA: setDiagnostics/getDiagnostics and any new overlay field — naive save() stores in ephemeral JSON only, lost on config regeneration","summary":"Implementing setDiagnostics(workspaceId, value) / getDiagnostics(workspaceId) by adding diagnostics to EMPTY() and LOCAL_FIELDS stores data in the overlay JSON file. That file is ephemeral — it can be wiped or regenerated, causing getDiagnostics to return null even after setDiagnostics was called. The durable path: (1) in emitDiff(), add a loop that calls graphStore.appendEvent(store, wsId, {evt:\"diagnostics_set\", value, ts}) for each changed diagnostics entry; (2) in graph-store.js switch, handle case \"diagnostics_set\": node.diagnostics = ev.value; (3) in overlay.js load(), rehydrate base.diagnostics[id] = node.diagnostics from the graph store nodes. Do NOT put diagnostics in LOCAL_FIELDS — that makes it ephemeral. Pattern already used for: assignee, timestamps, metrics, measurements. Discovered when setDiagnostics/getDiagnostics round-trip failed after overlay JSON deletion.","created_by":"bench-loop","valid_from":"2026-06-11T10:14:13.607Z","vec":[-0.039295025169849396,0.0820443257689476,-0.03424873203039169,0.09049572795629501,0.05287127569317818,-0.03441428020596504,-0.021712547168135643,0.029585788026452065,-0.05150051414966583,0.023948047310113907,0.07422208040952682,-0.025119829922914505,-0.016043009236454964,-0.013818858191370964,0.005041437689214945,0.02782297134399414,-0.0006099470192566514,-0.055512066930532455,-0.03647022321820259,-0.018740087747573853,-0.020450260490179062,-0.003964895848184824,0.0054933661594986916,0.04061378538608551,0.03363097459077835,0.02773587591946125,-0.06320521235466003,0.013215390034019947,0.002449911553412676,-0.0023697270080447197,0.007676407229155302,0.030400749295949936,-0.046680692583322525,0.01646951213479042,0.05947374925017357,0.06666302680969238,0.02330305054783821,0.02315